  "question": {
    "text": "P and Q combines to form two compounds $\\mathrm{PQ}_2$ and $\\mathrm{PQ}_3$. If $1 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{P} Q_2$ is dissolved in 51 g benzene the depression of freezing point becomes $0.8^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. On the other hand if $1 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{PQ}_3$ is dissolved in 51 g of benzene, the depression of freezing point becomes $0.625^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$. The atomic mass of $P$ and $Q$ are $\\left(\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{f}}\\right.$ of benzene $\\left.=5.1 \\mathrm{~K} \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
